  "Obtain the [events] needed to admit a [47m[defabsstobj][0m event

  We assume familiarity with [47m[defabsstobj][0m.  [47mDefabsstobj-missing-events[0m
  is a macro is for advanced users (who, for example, understand the
  role of the [47mtranslate[0m and [47muntranslate[0m functions), who want
  programmatic access to the [47m[defthm][0m events required to admit a
  specific [47mdefabsstobj[0m event.

  This macro has the same syntax as [47m[defabsstobj][0m --- to use it, just
  replace a call of [47m[defabsstobj][0m by a call of
  [47mdefabsstobj-missing-events[0m on the same arguments.  The result is an
  error triple [47m(mv erp val state)[0m.  If [47merp[0m is [47mnil[0m, then [47mval[0m is the
  list of all objects [47m(name formula . old-formula)[0m, where a [47m[defthm][0m
  event named [47mname[0m remains to be admitted whose translated formula is
  [47mformula[0m, and where [47mold-formula[0m is [47mnil[0m unless the indicated event
  already exists (hence with a different formula), in which case
  [47mold-formula[0m is the existing translated formula.

