 (DEFTHEORY-STATIC
  (EVENTS THEORIES)
  "Define a `static' theory (to [enable] or [disable] a set of rules)

  This macro provides a variant of [47m[deftheory][0m, such that the resulting
  theory is the same at [47m[include-book][0m time as it was at
  [47m[certify-book][0m time.

  We assume that the reader is familiar with [theories]; see
  [deftheory].  We begin here by illustrating how [47mdeftheory-static[0m
  differs from [47m[deftheory][0m.  Suppose for example that the following
  events are the first two events in a book, where that book is
  certified in the initial ACL2 [world] (see [ground-zero]).

    (deftheory my-theory
      (current-theory :here))
    (deftheory-static my-static-theory
      (current-theory :here))

  Now suppose we include that book after executing the following event.

    (in-theory (disable car-cons))

  Suppose that later we execute [47m(in-theory (theory 'my-theory))[0m.  Then
  the rule [47mcar-cons[0m will be disabled, because it was disabled at the
  time the expression [47m(current-theory :here)[0m was evaluated when
  processing the [47mdeftheory[0m of [47mmy-theory[0m while including the book.
  However, if we execute [47m(in-theory (theory 'my-static-theory))[0m, then
  the rule [47mcar-cons[0m will be enabled, because the value of the theory
  [47mmy-static-theory[0m was saved at the time the book was certified.

    General Form:
    (deftheory-static name term)

  The arguments are handled the same as for [47m[deftheory][0m.  Thus, [47mname[0m is
  a new symbolic name (see [name]), and [47mterm[0m is a term that when
  evaluated will produce a theory (see [theories]).  Except for the
  variable [47m[world][0m, [47mterm[0m must contain no free variables.  [47mTerm[0m is
  evaluated with [47m[world][0m bound to the current world (see [world]) and
  the resulting theory is then converted to a [3mrunic theory[0m (see
  [theories]) and associated with [47mname[0m.  Henceforth, this runic
  theory is returned as the value of the theory expression [47m(theory
  name)[0m.

  As for [47m[deftheory][0m, the value returned is the length of the resulting
  theory.

  We conclude with an optional discussion about the implementation of
  [47mdeftheory-static[0m, for those familiar with [47m[make-event][0m.  The
  following macroexpansion of the [47mdeftheory-static[0m form above shows
  how this works (see [trans1]).

    ACL2 !>:trans1 (deftheory-static my-static-theory
                     (current-theory :here))
     (MAKE-EVENT (LET ((WORLD (W STATE)))
                      (LIST 'DEFTHEORY
                            'MY-STATIC-THEORY
                            (LIST 'QUOTE (CURRENT-THEORY :HERE)))))
    ACL2 !>

  The idea is that upon evaluation of this [47mmake-event[0m form, the first
  step is to evaluate the indicated [47m[let][0m expression to obtain a form
  [47m(deftheory my-theory '(...))[0m, where ``[47m(...)[0m'' is a list of all
  [rune]s in current theory.  If this form is in a book being
  certified, then the resulting [47mdeftheory[0m form is stored in the
  book's certificate, and is used when the book is included later.")
