            :rule-classes rule-classes
            :instructions instructions
            :hints        hints
            :otf-flg      otf-flg)

  where [47mname[0m is a new symbolic name (see [name]), [47mterm[0m is a term
  alleged to be a theorem, and [47m[rule-classes][0m, [47m[instructions][0m,
  [47m[hints][0m, and [47m[otf-flg][0m are as described in their respective
  [documentation].  The keyword arguments above are all optional,
  however you may not supply both [47m:[0m[47m[instructions][0m and [47m:[0m[47m[hints][0m, since
  one drives the interactive [proof-builder] and the other drives the
  theorem prover.  If [47m:[0m[47m[rule-classes][0m is not specified, the list
  [47m(:rewrite)[0m is used; if you wish the theorem to generate no rules,
  specify [47m:[0m[47m[rule-classes][0m [47mnil[0m.

  When ACL2 processes a [47mdefthm[0m event, it first tries to prove the
  [term] using the indicated hints (see [hints]) or [instructions]
  (see [proof-builder]).  If it is successful, it stores the rules
  described by the rule-classes (see [rule-classes]), proving the
  necessary corollaries.


