  (APPLY$ ACL2-BUILT-INS)
  "Issue a warrant for a function so [47m[apply$][0m can use it in proofs

  It is best to be somewhat familiar with the documentation of [47m[apply$][0m
  before reading this topic.

  Before using [47mdefwarrant[0m or a utility like [47m[defun$][0m that relies on it:

    (include-book \"projects/apply/top\" :dir :system)

  Several lemmas in that book are necessary for [47mdefwarrant[0m to prove the
  theorems it must prove.


Badges versus Warrants

  It is easy to confuse [badge]s, which are issued by [47m[defbadge][0m, with
  [warrant]s, which are issued by [47mdefwarrant[0m.  See the first section
  of [47m[defbadge][0m for an extended discussion.


Requirements of [47mDefwarrant[0m

    General Form:
    (defwarrant fn)

  where [47mfn[0m is a defined function name.  This command analyzes the body
  of [47mfn[0m to determine whether it satisfies certain stringent syntactic
  and semantic conditions that allow the ACL2 proof theory to be
  extended so that the prover can simplify forms like [47m(apply$ 'fn
  ...)[0m.  The syntactic conditions include those of [47m[defbadge][0m, which
  [47mdefwarrant[0m essentially invokes if [47mfn[0m is a [47m:[0m[47m[logic][0m mode function
  that is not already badged.  But below we describe all the
  conditions checked by [47mdefwarrant[0m since many users use [47mdefwarrant[0m to
  issue both a badge and a warrant.

  Basic conditions include that [47mfn[0m is in [47m:[0m[47m[logic][0m-mode and that its
  justification (i.e., the measure, well-founded relation, and domain
  predicate used to admit [47mfn[0m) be expressible without any reference to
  [47m[apply$][0m, [47m[ev$][0m, or [47m[apply$-userfn][0m.

  [47mDefwarrant[0m imposes some additional conditions on [47mfn[0m, but exactly what
  those conditions are depends on a certain ``reachability'' test
  detailed in the section titled [31;1mThe ``Reachability'' Test[0m in
  [47m[defbadge][0m.  Roughly speaking the test is whether [47mapply$[0m is
  ancestral in [47mfn[0m, meaning [47mapply$[0m is somehow involved in the
  definition of [47mfn[0m or the functions it calls.

  If the reachability test succeeds --- colloquially, if [47mfn[0m depends on
  [47mapply$[0m --- then [47mdefwarrant[0m imposes the following additional
  conditions in order to issue a warrant.

  [3m(a)[0m If [47mfn[0m is recursive it must not be part of a mutually recursive
  clique and its measure must be of type [47m[natp][0m or be a lexicographic
  combination of natural numbers as defined by the [47mllist[0m function in
  the Community Books at [47mbooks/ordinals/[0m.

  [3m(b)[0m Every function called in the body of [47mfn[0m, except [47mfn[0m itself, must
  already have a [badge] and a warrant.  If some subfunction doesn't
  already have a badge, [47mdefwarrant[0m will call [47m[defbadge][0m and signal an
  error if that fails.  If some subfunction doesn't already have a
  warrant, [47mdefwarrant[0m will signal an error and suggest that you call
  [47mdefwarrant[0m on the offending subfunction first.  [47mDefwarrant[0m will
  continue to fail until all subfunctions have badges and warrants.

  [3m(c)[0m It must be possible for each formal of [47mfn[0m to be assigned one of
  three [ilk]s, [47m:FN[0m, [47m:EXPR[0m, or [47mNIL[0m, as described below.  The basic
  idea is that a formal can be assigned ilk [47m:FN[0m (or ilk [47m:EXPR[0m) iff it
  is sometimes passed into a [47m:FN[0m (or [47m:EXPR[0m) slot in the body of [47mfn[0m
  and is never passed into any other kind of slot.  A formal can be
  be assigned ilk [47mNIL[0m iff it is never passed into a slot of ilk [47m:FN[0m
  or [47m:EXPR[0m, i.e., if it is used as an ``ordinary'' object.  We are
  more precise below.

  [3m(d)[0m Every [47m:FN[0m and [47m:EXPR[0m slot of every function called in the body of
  [47mfn[0m is occupied either by a formal of [47mfn[0m of the same ilk or, in the
  case of calls of functions other than [47mfn[0m, a quoted [tame] function
  symbol or quoted tame (preferably well-formed) [47mLAMBDA[0m object.

  This completes the list of additional restrictions imposed by
  [47mdefwarrant[0m on [47mfn[0m, when [47mapply$[0m is reachable from [47mfn[0m.

  If the reachability test fails --- colloquially, if [47mfn[0m does not
  depend on [47mapply$[0m --- then [47mdefwarrant[0m just checks that [47mfn[0m does not
  call any of a few functions that [47mapply$[0m is prohibited from running.
  Among those blacklisted functions are [47m[sys-call][0m and other
  functions requiring a trust tag.  For a list of the blacklisted
