  (THEORIES THEORY-FUNCTIONS)
  "Deletes names from current theory

    Example:
    (disable fact (:e fact) associativity-of-app)

    General Form:
    (disable name1 name2 ... namek)

  where each [47mnamei[0m is a runic designator; see [theories].  The result
  is the theory that contains all the names in the current theory
  except those listed.  Note that this is merely a function that
  returns a theory.  The result is generally a very long list of
  [rune]s and you will probably regret printing it.

  For related utilities, see [enable] and see [e/d].

  The standard way to ``disable'' a fixed set of names, is as follows;
  see [hints] and see [in-theory].

    :in-theory (disable name1 name2 ... namek)    ; in a hint
    (in-theory (disable name1 name2 ... namek))   ; as an event
    (local ; often desirable, to avoid exporting from the current context
     (in-theory (disable name1 name2 ... namek)))

  Note that all the names are implicitly quoted.  If you wish to
  disable a computed list of names, [47mlst[0m, use the theory expression
  [47m(set-difference-theories (current-theory :here) lst)[0m.

