  a function symbol [47mFN[0m is introduced, evaluate [47m(disabledp 'FN)[0m.")
 (DISABLE-FORCING
  (FORCE)
  "To disallow forced case-splits

    General Form:
    ACL2 !>:disable-forcing   ; disallow forced case splits

  See [force] and see [case-split] for a discussion of forced case
  splits, which are inhibited by this command.

  [47mDisable-forcing[0m is actually a macro that [disable]s the
  [executable-counterpart] of the function symbol [47mforce[0m; see [force].
  When you want to use [hints] to turn off forced case splits, use a
  form such as one of the following (these are equivalent).

    :in-theory (disable (:executable-counterpart force))
    :in-theory (disable (force))

  The following example shows how this works.  First evaluate these
  forms.

    (defstub f1 (x) t)
    (defstub f2 (x) t)
    (defaxiom ax (implies (case-split (f2 x)) (f1 x)))
    (thm (f1 x))

  You will see the application of the rule, [47max[0m, in the proof of the
  [47m[thm][0m call above.  However, if you first evaluate
  [47m(disable-forcing)[0m, then there will be no application of [47max[0m.  To
  restore forced case splitting, see [enable-forcing].")
