  (EQUAL EQUALITY-VARIANTS ACL2-BUILT-INS)
  "Equality of symbols

  [47mEq[0m is the function for determining whether two objects are identical
  (i.e., have the exact same store address in the current von Neumann
  implementation of Common Lisp).  It is the same as [47m[equal][0m in the
  ACL2 logic.

  [47mEq[0m is a Common Lisp function.  In order to ensure conformance with
  Common Lisp, the ACL2 [guard] on [47meq[0m requires at least one of the
  arguments to [47meq[0m to be a symbol.  Common Lisp guarantees that if [47mx[0m
  is a symbol, then [47mx[0m is [47meq[0m to [47my[0m if and only if [47mx[0m is [47m[equal][0m to [47my[0m.
  Thus, the ACL2 user should think of [47meq[0m as nothing besides a fast
  means for checking [47m[equal][0m when one argument is known to be a
