 (EV$
  (APPLY$)
  "Evaluate a tame expression using [47mapply$[0m

  When [47m[apply$][0m, actually [47m[apply$-lambda][0m, is asked to apply a [47mLAMBDA[0m
  object to some arguments it calls [47mev$[0m on the body of the object and
  an alist binding the formals of the object to the arguments.
  Roughly put, [47mev$[0m ``works'' by looking up symbols, returning quoted
  objects, and using [47mapply$[0m to apply function symbols to the results
  of evaluating their arguments.  [47mEv$[0m and its clique-mate [47mev$-list[0m
  are mutually-recursive with [47mapply$[0m.  [47mEv$[0m can only evaluate ``as
  expected'' on [tame] expressions and requires [47m[warrant][0ms, explicit
  in the proof theory or implicit in the evaluation theory, to
  determine [badge]s and thus tameness.  See [47m[apply$][0m for details,
  including the formal definitions of [47mev$[0m and [47mev$-list[0m.  For a
  summary of how the rewriter handles [47mapply$[0m, [47mev$[0m, and [47mloop$[0m
  [scion]s, see [rewriting-calls-of-apply$-ev$-and-loop$-scions].")
