        is no reason to include an [47m:ERROR[0m hint in any user-typein,
        since it will only cause an error when the form is evaluated.
        [47m:ERROR[0m hints are useful in the definition of functions that
        generate custom keyword hints (see [custom-keyword-hints])
        and computed hints (see [computed-hints]).  For example, if
        you wish to define a custom keyword hint [47m:my-hint val[0m and you
        wish the hint to signal an error if there is something
        inappropriate about [47mval[0m in the context of the hint, use the
        following code to generate the hint

          (list :ERROR (cons \"Your specified value, ~x0, is inappropriate\"
                             (list (cons #0 val))))

        which is equivalent to

          (list :ERROR (msg \"Your specified value, ~x0, is inappropriate\"
                            val))

        which, if [47mval[0m has the value [47m123[0m, would evaluate to the hint

          (:ERROR (\"Your specified value, ~x0, is inappropriate\" (#0 . 123))).

        Note that any time an [47m:ERROR[0m keyword is produced during hint
        processing, including iterations of the expansions of custom
        keyword hints or of [override-hints], an error will occur.

