    (defthm lemma1 ...)
    (defthm lemma2 ...)
    (i-am-here)
    The following lemma won't go through.  I started
    typing the hint but realized I need to prove a
    lemma first.  See the failed proof attempt in foo.bar.
    I'm going to quit for the night now and resume tomorrow
    from home.

    (defthm lemma3 ...
      :hints ((\"Goal\" :use (:instance ???
    ...

  By putting an [47m(i-am-here)[0m form at the ``frontier'' of an evolving
  file of [command]s, you can use [47m[rebuild][0m to load the file up to
  the [47m(i-am-here)[0m.  [47mI-am-here[0m simply returns an [error-triple] that
  indicates an error, and any form that ``causes an error'' will do
