  "Number of bits in two's complement integer representation

  For non-negative integers, [47m(integer-length i)[0m is the minimum number
  of bits needed to represent the integer.  Any integer can be
  represented as a signed two's complement field with a minimum of [47m(+
  (integer-length i) 1)[0m bits.

  The [guard] for [47minteger-length[0m requires its argument to be an
