  [47m(Keywordp x)[0m is true if and only if [47mx[0m is a keyword, i.e., a symbol in
  the \"KEYWORD\" package.  Such symbols are typically printed using a
  colon (:) followed by the [47m[symbol-name][0m of the symbol.

  [47mKeywordp[0m has a [guard] of [47mt[0m.

  [47mKeywordp[0m is a Common Lisp function.  See any Common Lisp
  documentation for more information.  The following log may be
