  function introduced in the [47m:partial-theory[0m of a dependent
  clause-processor is not instantiable; see
  [define-trusted-clause-processor].)  A pseudo-lambda expression is
  an expression of the form [47m(lambda (v1 ... vn) body)[0m where the [47mvi[0m
  are distinct variable symbols and [47mbody[0m is any term.  No [3ma priori[0m
  relation is imposed between the [47mvi[0m and the variables of [47mbody[0m, i.e.,
  [47mbody[0m may ignore some [47mvi[0m's and may contain ``free'' variables.
  However, we do not permit [47mv[0m to occur freely in [47mbody[0m if the
