  Consider the application of [47m:termination-theorem f[0m while attempting
  to prove the termination theorem for a function, [47mg[0m.  For now
  suppose that neither [47mf[0m nor [47mg[0m is defined using [47m[mutual-recursion][0m.
  Suppose that [47mf[0m and [47mg[0m have the same number of formal parameters.
  Then every call of [47mf[0m in the termination theorem for [47mf[0m will be
  replaced by a call of [47mg[0m on the same arguments (except, recursively,
  [47mf[0m is also replaced by [47mg[0m in those arguments).  The analogous
  replacement also takes place for mutually recursive definitions, as
  follows.  In the case that [47mf[0m was introduced with [47m(mutual-recursion
  (defun f1 ...) ... (defun fk ...))[0m and similarly [47mg[0m is being
  introduced with [47m(mutual-recursion (defun g1 ...)  ... (defun gk
  ...))[0m, where for each [47mi[0m from [47m1[0m to [47mk[0m the number of formal parameters
