  theorem for [47mf[0m.  If that argument is supplied, then there will be no
  attempt to derive a functional substitution automatically, as
  described in the preceding paragraph.

  (7) [47m(:guard-theorem name)[0m or [47m(:guard-theorem name simplify)[0m, where
  [47mname[0m is a [guard]-verified function symbol (hence, in particular,
  is in [logic] mode).  Such a lemma instance denotes the guard
  theorem previously proved for [47mname[0m, where by default [47msimplify[0m is
  [47m:limited[0m, which enables certain simplifications as documented
  elsewhere; see [gthm].  Otherwise [47msimplify[0m should be [47mnil[0m, to avoid
  all such simplification.  If [47mname[0m is defined as part of a
  mutually-recursive clique of definitions (see [mutual-recursion]),
  then the lemma instance refers to the guard theorem proved for the
