  "Challenge Proof Problems for [47mDO[0m [47mLoop$[0ms


LP17: Challenge Proof Problems for [47mDO[0m [47mLoop$[0ms

  In the following problems please write [47mDO[0m [47mloop$[0ms even though some of
  the problems can be solved with [47mFOR[0m [47mloop$[0ms.

  Our answers to the problems in this section are in [community-books]
  file [47mdemos/loop-primer/lp17.lisp[0m.

------------------------------
  [31;1mLP17-1:[0m Write a [47mDO[0m [47mloop$[0m that reverses the list [47mlst[0m.  For example, if
  [47mlst[0m is [47m(A B C)[0m the result should be [47m(C B A)[0m.  Prove that your [47mDO[0m
  [47mloop$[0m is equal to [47m(rev lst)[0m, where

    (defun rev (x)
      (if (endp x)
          nil
          (append (rev (cdr x)) (list (car x)))))

------------------------------
  [31;1mLP17-2:[0m Write a [47mDO[0m [47mloop$[0m that computes [47m(member e lst)[0m and prove it
  correct.

  [31;1mHint:[0m Sometimes the main theorem suggests the right induction on its
  own.

------------------------------
  [31;1mLP17-3:[0m Prove the following:

    (defthm lp17-3-main
      (equal (loop$ with x = lst
                    with ans = 0
                    do
                     (cond ((endp x) (return ans))
                           (t (progn (setq ans (+ 1 ans))
                                     (setq x (cdr x))))))
             (len lst)))

------------------------------
  [31;1mLP17-4:[0m Write a [47mDO[0m [47mloop$[0m that computes [47m(nth n lst)[0m, when [47mn[0m is a
  natural number.  Prove it correct.

------------------------------
  [31;1mLP17-5:[0m Prove the following.

    (defthm lp17-5-main
      (implies (true-listp lst)
               (equal (loop$ with x = lst
                             with ans = nil
                             do
                             (cond
                              ((endp x) (return ans))
                              (t (progn (setq ans (append ans (list (car x))))
                                        (setq x (cdr x))))))
                      lst)))

------------------------------
  [31;1mLP17-6:[0m Prove the following.

    (defthm lp17-6-main
      (implies (and (natp m)
                    (natp n))
               (equal (loop$ with i = m
                             with j = n
                             do
                             (if (zp i)
                                 (return j)
                                 (progn (setq i (- i 1))
                                        (setq j (+ j 1)))))
                      (+ m n))))

------------------------------
  [31;1mLP17-7:[0m Write a [47mDO[0m [47mloop$[0m that computes [47m(fact n)[0m, for natural number
  [47mn[0m, where

    (defun fact (n)
      (if (zp n)
          1
          (* n (fact (- n 1)))))

------------------------------
  [31;1mLP17-8:[0m Write a [47mDO[0m [47mloop$[0m that scans a list of numbers, [47mlst[0m, once and
  returns the sum of the elements and the sum of the squares (with [47msq[0m
  as defined below) of the elements of [47mlst[0m as a cons pair.  E.g.,
  given [47m(1 2 3 4 5)[0m return [47m(cons (+ 1 2 3 4 5) (+ (sq 1) (sq 2) (sq
  3) (sq 4) (sq 5)))[0m = [47m(15 . 55)[0m.

  Prove that your do loop$ is equal to

    (cons (loop$ for e in lst sum e)
          (loop$ for e in lst sum (sq e)))

  Use the following definition of [47msq[0m.

    (defun sq (x) (* x x))

------------------------------
  [31;1mLP17-9:[0m Define [47m(partition-symbols lst)[0m with a [47mDO[0m [47mloop$[0m that
  partitions [47mlst[0m into two lists, one containing all the symbols in
