  (LOOP$-PRIMER)
  "Syntax of [47mFOR[0m [47mLoop$[0ms


LP4: Syntax of [47mFOR[0m [47mLoop$[0ms

  To describe the syntax of [47mFOR[0m [47mloop$[0ms we first describe the most
  elaborate [47mFOR[0m [47mloop$[0m.  Then we note which elements can be omitted.
  The most elaborate [47mFOR[0m [47mloop$[0m is of the form

  [47m(LOOP$ FOR [0m[3mv1[0m[47m OF-TYPE [0m[3mspec1 target1[0m
  [47mAS [0m   [3mv2[0m[47m OF-TYPE [0m[3mspec2 target2[0m
  ...
  [47mAS [0m   [3mvn[0m[47m OF-TYPE [0m[3mspecn targetn[0m
  [47mUNTIL :GUARD [0m[3mguard1 until-expr[0m
  [47mWHEN [0m   [47m:GUARD [0m[3mguard2 when-expr[0m
  [3mop[0m[47m :GUARD [0m[3mguard3 body-expr[0m[47m)[0m

  where

    * each [3mvi[0m   is a legal variable symbol, they are all distinct, and are
      collectively called the [3miteration variables[0m,

    * each [3mspeci[0m   is a [47m[type-spec][0m for the corresponding variable [3mvi[0m,

    * each [3mtargeti[0m is of one of the forms below and specifies the range of
      values to be taken by the corresponding variable [3mvi[0m.
      Abstractly you may think of the ``range'' here simply as a list
      of the values as described below, where [3mlist-expr[0m is a term
      (which is expected to evaluate to a true list), [3mlo-expr[0m and
      [3mhi-expr[0m are terms (which are expected to evaluate to integers),
      and [3mstep-expr[0m is a term (which is expected to evaluate to a
      positive integer).  In the examples given below, let [47mrv[0m be the
      list reverse function, so [47m(rv '(a b c))[0m is [47m(C B A)[0m.

        * [47mIN[0m [3mlist-expr[0m --- range is the value of [3mlist-expr[0m.  For example, the
          range of ``[47mIN[0m [47m(rv '(a b c))[0m'' is [47m(C B A)[0m.

        * [47mON[0m [3mlist-expr[0m --- range is the list of successive non-[47mnil[0m tails of the
          value of [3mlist-expr[0m.  For example, the range of ``[47mON[0m [47m(rv '(a
          b c))[0m'' is [47m((C B A) (B A) (A))[0m.  The range value is
          produced by [47m(TAILS [0m[3mlist-expr[0m[47m)[0m.

        * [47mFROM[0m [3mlo-expr[0m [47mTO[0m [3mhi-expr[0m [47mBY[0m [3mstep-expr[0m --- If ``[47mBY[0m [3mstep-expr[0m'' is
          omitted, ``[47mBY 1[0m'' is used.  The range contains all the
          integers from the value of [3mlo-expr[0m to the greatest integer
          less than or equal to the value of [3mhi-expr[0m such that each
          is separated from its higher neighbor by the value of
          [3mstep-expr[0m.  For example, the range of ``[47mFROM[0m 1 [47mTO[0m 10 [47mBY[0m 2''
          is [47m(1 3 5 7 9)[0m.  The range value is produced by [47m(FROM-TO-BY
          [0m[3mlo-expr[0m [3mhi-expr[0m [3mstep-expr[0m[47m)[0m.

    * each [3mguardi[0m is a term,

    * each [3muntil-expr[0m, [3mwhen-expr[0m, and [3mbody-expr[0m   is a [47m[tame][0m term, and

    * [3mop[0m   is one of the [3moperators[0m   [47mSUM[0m, [47mCOLLECT[0m, [47mAPPEND[0m, [47mALWAYS[0m, or
      [47mTHEREIS[0m.

  The symbols [47mFOR[0m, [47mIN[0m, [47mON[0m, [47mFROM[0m, [47mTO[0m, [47mBY[0m, [47mOF-TYPE[0m, [47mWHEN[0m, [47mUNTIL[0m, [47mSUM[0m,
  [47mCOLLECT[0m, [47mAPPEND[0m, [47mALWAYS[0m, and [47mTHEREIS[0m when used in [47mloop$[0m statements
  may be in any package.

  Common Lisp prohibits loops with both a [47mWHEN[0m clause and either an
  [47mALWAYS[0m or a [47mTHEREIS[0m operator.  For example, if you are tempted to
  write ``[47mWHEN[0m [3mp[0m [47mALWAYS[0m [3mq[0m'' you can instead write ``[47mALWAYS[0m [47m(if [0m[3mp q[0m
  [47mt)[0m.''

  The following elements may be omitted from the most elaborate form
  and still produce legal [47mloop$[0m statements:

    * any line beginning with [47mAS[0m, [47mUNTIL[0m or [47mWHEN[0m,

    * any [47mOF-TYPE[0m [3mspeci[0m, and

    * any [47m:GUARD[0m [3mguardi[0m.

  A [47mFOR[0m [47mloop$[0m expression with just one iteration variable and in which
  the iterative expressions mention no free variable other than the
  iteration variable is called a [3msimple [47mloop$[0m[3m[0m (or, sometimes, a
  [3msimple loop[0m).  An example of a simple loop is

    (loop$ for x in lst when (evenp x) collect (+ 1 (sq x))).

  A [47mFOR[0m [47mloop$[0m expression is called a [3mfancy [47mloop$[0m[3m[0m if it is not simple.
  Both of the following [47mloop$[0ms are fancy.

    (loop$ for x in xlst as y on ylst collect (expr x y))

    (loop$ for x in xlst collect (expr x z))

  The first is fancy because it has two iteration variables, [47mx[0m and [47my[0m.
  The second is fancy because the body freely uses the variable [47mz[0m
  which is not the iteration variable.

  Now go to [lp-section-5] (or return to the Table of Contents (see
  [LP-SECTION-0])).")
