 (MAGIC-EV-FNCALL
  (META)
  "Call the named function on the given arguments and return the value.

  Introduction.  [47mMagic-ev-fncall[0m is a [logic]-mode function that can
  apply a given function (which need not be in logic mode) to an
  argument list.  Although the result can be computed,
  [47mmagic-ev-fncall[0m is technically a constrained function (with unknown
  constraints), which can be assumed in metafunctions and [clause]
  processors to produce correct results, via [meta-extract].

  Examples:

    (magic-ev-fncall 'cons '(3 4) state t nil)
      = (mv nil '(3 . 4))
    (magic-ev-fncall (car '(floor foo)) (list (+ 6 7) 5) state t nil)
      = (mv nil 2)

  General Form:

    (magic-ev-fncall fn arglist state hard-error-returns-nilp aokp)

  where [47mfn[0m is a function symbol, [47marglist[0m is a suitable argument list
  for [47mfn[0m, and the last two formals are described below.  When
  successful, the result is [47m(mv nil value)[0m where [47mvalue[0m is the
  application of [47mfn[0m to [47marglist[0m.  Although this fact cannot be proven,
  it may be assumed correct in metafunctions and clause processors
  via [meta-extract], assuming of course that [47mfn[0m is a [logic]-mode
  function.

  In general, the result is either [47m(mv t error-msg)[0m (if, e.g., the
  function was not defined, the arity was wrong, or the guards were
  violated) or [47m(mv nil value)[0m on success.  In the case of a
  [multiple-value]d function the second return value is the list of
  values.  A non-nil error message, [47merror-msg[0m, is a message suitable
  for printing with [47m[fmt][0m; see [msg].

  If a hard error is encountered during execution and
  [47mhard-error-returns-nilp[0m is non-[47mnil[0m, then the error is ignored and
  the value returned is [47m(mv nil nil)[0m (note that the logical value of
  a call of [47mHARD-ERROR[0m is [47mnil[0m).  If [47mhard-error-returns-nilp[0m is [47mnil[0m
  then the return value is of the form [47m(mv T error-msg)[0m.

  The [47maokp[0m argument controls whether attachments to constrained
  functions may be executed (see [defattach]).  If [47mnil[0m, then an error
  message is returned when an attachment would otherwise be executed.

  When used in a clause-processor or metafunction, it can be assumed
  via a [meta-extract] hypothesis that [47mmagic-ev-fncall[0m works
  correctly with respect to the evaluator, but only if
  [47mhard-error-returns-nilp[0m is [47mt[0m and [47maokp[0m is [47mnil[0m.

  The [guard] for [47m(magic-ev-fncall fn arglist state h aokp)[0m is [47mt[0m, but
  evaluation of this call enforces the following requirements.

    * [47mFn[0m must be a function symbol of the current ACL2 [world] other than
      [47mif[0m, whose arity is equal to the length of the true-list,
      [47marglist[0m.

    * [47mFn[0m must not have any [47mstobj[0m inputs or be a stobj creator.

    * Calls of [47mfn[0m must not require a trust tag (see [defttag]).

    * [47mFn[0m must not be untouchable (see [push-untouchable]).

  The implementation of these checks incorporates a bit of trickery so
  that they are reasonably efficient.

  Note that [47m[set-guard-checking][0m affects evaluation of calls of
  [47m(magic-ev-fncall fn ...)[0m just as it affects calls of [47mfn[0m, for
  example as follows.

    ACL2 !>(magic-ev-fncall 'car '((a b c)) state t nil)
    (NIL A)
    ACL2 !>(magic-ev-fncall 'car '(3) state t nil)
    (T <... message elided here ...>)
    ACL2 !>(set-guard-checking nil)

    Masking guard violations but still checking guards except for self-
    recursive calls.  To avoid guard checking entirely, :SET-GUARD-CHECKING
    :NONE.  See :DOC set-guard-checking.

    ACL2 >(magic-ev-fncall 'car '(3) state t nil)
    (NIL NIL)
    ACL2 >

  Additional Notes.

    * If [47mfn[0m is a [program]-mode function, then the call will be evaluated
      under [safe-mode], which avoids raw Lisp errors due to calls of
      ill-[guard]ed program-mode functions.

    * If the application of [47mfn[0m returns multiple values [47m(mv v1 v2 ...)[0m, then
      the resulting value will be the corresponding list [47m(v1 v2 ...)[0m.

    * A reasonable model for [47m(magic-ev-fncall 'fn (list a1 a2 ...) state h
      aokp)[0m is [47m(ec-call (fn a1 a2 ...))[0m.")
