  "Introduce a guard proof obligation

  The macro [47mmbt*[0m is a variant of [47mmbt[0m (``must be true'').  However,
  unlike [47mmbt[0m, the call [47m(mbt* test)[0m is equivalent simply to [47mt[0m for both
  logic and evaluation.  The only effective difference between [47m(mbt*
  test)[0m and [47mt[0m is that [47m(mbt* test)[0m generates a [guard] proof
  obligation (when used in a [47m[logic][0m-mode definition) of [47mtest[0m.

