  Two non-[47mnil[0m values are allowed for keyword parameter [47m:ideal-okp[0m:
  [47m:warn[0m and [47mt[0m.  Both of these values allow memoization of ideal-mode
  functions, but if [47m:warn[0m is supplied then a warning will take place
  at memoization time, specifically for the resulting [table] event.
  Note that you may set the key [47m:memoize-ideal-okp[0m of the
  [47m[ACL2-defaults-table][0m to value [47mt[0m or [47m:warn[0m to change the default,
  but if parameter [47m:ideal-okp[0m is supplied, the [47m[ACL2-defaults-table][0m
  value is ignored.

  The value of [47m:verbose[0m is [47mnil[0m by default, which avoids output that is
  typically distracting.  Otherwise [47mverbose[0m should be [47mt[0m.  We can see
  the types of output that are inhibited by default by using
  [47m:[0m[47m[trans1][0m as follows follows (most output elided here); see
