  Logically, this function just returns [47mnil[0m.  But execution of
  [47m(never-memoize fn)[0m records that [47mfn[0m must never be memoized, so that
  any attempt to memoize [47mfn[0m will fail.

  Any function can be marked as unsafe to memoize; in fact, [47mfn[0m need not
  even be defined at the time it is marked.

  This is useful for prohibiting the memoization of functions that are
  known to involve destructive functions like [47mnreverse[0m.")
