 (OBSERVATION
  (IO ACL2-BUILT-INS)
  "Print an observation

  Here is a typical application of [47mobservation[0m.

    ACL2 !>(let ((ctx 'top-level)
                 (name 'foo))
             (observation ctx
                          \"Skipping processing of name ~x0.\"
                          name))

    ACL2 Observation in TOP-LEVEL:  Skipping processing of name FOO.
    <state>
    ACL2 !>

  [47mObservation[0m prints an initial ``[47mACL2 Observation...: [0m'', and then
  prints the indicated message using formatted printing (see [fmt]).
  Notice in the example above that evaluation of a call of
  [47mobservation[0m returns [47m[state][0m.  Indeed, [47mobservation[0m is actually a
  macro whose expansion takes and returns the ACL2 [47m[state][0m.  A
  similar utility, [47mobservation-cw[0m, is available that does not take or
  return [47mstate[0m; rather, it returns [47mnil[0m as the suffix ``[47mcw[0m'' suggests
  that a ``comment window'' is the target of this printing, rather
  than the state.  For example:

    ACL2 !>(let ((ctx 'top-level)
                 (name 'foo))
             (observation-cw ctx
                             \"Skipping processing of name ~x0.\"
                             name))

    ACL2 Observation in TOP-LEVEL:  Skipping processing of name FOO.
    NIL
    ACL2 !>

  [47mObservation-cw[0m takes exactly the same arguments as [47mobservation[0m, but
  [47mobservation-cw[0m does its printing in a so-called ``wormhole''; see
  [wormhole].

    General Forms:
    (observation    ctx fmt-string fmt-arg1 fmt-arg2 ... fmt-argk)
    (observation-cw ctx fmt-string fmt-arg1 fmt-arg2 ... fmt-argk)

  where [47mctx[0m generally evaluates to a symbol (but see below), and
  [47mfmt-string[0m together with the [47mfmt-argi[0m are suitable for passing to
  [47m[fmt][0m.  Output begins and ends with a newline.

  Recall from the example above that the output from a call of
  [47mobservation[0m (or [47mobservation-cw[0m) begins with ``[47mACL2 Observation[0m''
  and additional characters ending in ``[47m: [0m'', for example ``[47m in
  TOP-LEVEL: [0m'', followed by formatted output produced from
  [47mfmt-string[0m with the given [47mfmt-argi[0m.  The characters printed
  immediately following the string ``[47mACL2 Observation[0m'' depend on the
  value of [47mctx[0m.  If [47mctx[0m is [47mnil[0m, nothing is printed.  If [47mctx[0m is a
  non-[47mnil[0m symbol, it is printed using [47m[fmt][0m directive [47m~x[0m.  If [47mctx[0m is
  a [47m[cons][0m pair whose [47m[car][0m is a symbol, formatted printing is
  applied to the string \"(~x0 ~x1 ...)\", where [47m#\\0[0m and [47m#\\1[0m are bound
  respectively to that car and cdr.  Otherwise, [47mctx[0m is printed using
  [47m[fmt][0m directive [47m~@[0m.

  We next discuss situations in which printing is inhibited for
  [47mobservation[0m and [47mobservation-cw[0m.  No printing is done when
  [47mobservation[0m is among the inhibited output types; see
  [set-inhibit-output-lst].  Moreover, no printing is done by
  [47mobservation[0m during [47m[include-book][0m.  If you want to avoid printing
  from [47mobservation-cw[0m during [47m[include-book][0m, then you need to manage
  that yourself.")
