  other functions:

    (include-book \"misc/total-order\" :dir :system)

    (defun-sk none-below-2 (y)
      (forall r (implies (<< r y) (not (M r)))))

    (defun-sk min-M2 () (exists y (and (M y) (none-below-2 y))))

  The question is whether [47m(implies (some-M) (min-M2))[0m is a theorem.
  Can you prove it?  Can you disprove it? See
  [47m[solution-to-ACL2-quantifier-exercise-2][0m for a solution.


