  characters are [47m#\\a[0m, [47m#\\A[0m, [47m#\\Newline[0m and [47m#\\Space[0m.  It is actually
  possible in ACL2 to ``construct'' and ``deconstruct'' characters in
  terms of naturals.  For example, one can construct [47m#\\A[0m from [47m65[0m, the
  ASCII code for uppercase `A'.

