  "Recursion and Induction: The Definitional Principle

  Below we give a new definitional principle that subsumes the
  previously given Principle of Structural Recursion.

  The definition

  [47m(defun[0m [3mf[0m  [47m([0m[3mv_1[0m ... [3mv_n[0m[47m)[0m [3m\\beta[0m[47m)[0m

  is [3madmissible[0m  if and only if

   1. [3mf[0m  is a new function symbol,

   2. the [3mv_i[0m  are distinct variable symbols,

   3. [3m\\beta[0m  is a term that mentions no variable other than the [3mv_i[0m  and
      calls no new function symbol other than (possibly) [3mf[0m, and

   4. there is a term [3mm[0m  (called the [3mmeasure[0m) such that the following are
      theorems:

        * [3mOrdinal Conjecture[0m

          [47m(o-p[0m [3mm[0m[47m)[0m

        * [3mMeasure Conjecture(s)[0m  For each recursive call of [47m([0m[3mf a_1[0m ... [3ma_n[0m[47m)[0m in
          [3m\\beta[0m  and the conjunction [3mq[0m  of tests ruling it,

          [47m(implies[0m [3mq[0m  [47m(o<[0m [3mm[0m/[3m\\sigma[0m  [3mm[0m[47m))[0m

          where [3m\\sigma[0m  is [47m{[0m[3mv_1[0m<--[3ma_1[0m,  ... , [3mv_n[0m<--[3ma_n[0m[47m}[0m.

  If that definition is admissible, then it adds the axiom:

  [47m([0m[3mf[0m  [3mv_1[0m ... [3mv_n[0m[47m) = [0m[3m\\beta[0m.

  In each of the problems below, admit the proposed definition, i.e.,
  identify the measure and prove the required theorems.

  (Maybe explore <<[47m[defun][0m>>?  Note in particular how the user can
  explicitly specify the measure and well-founded relation alleged to
  decrease.  When specified, the system will attempt to prove it
  decreases as per the Definitional Principle.  If no measure is
  specified by the user, the system attempts to find an argument
  whose [47m[ACL2-count][0m decreases according to [47m[o<][0m.)

