  (see [R-AND-I-TABLE-OF-CONTENTS]))")
 (R-AND-I-SUBSTITUTIONS
  (RECURSION-AND-INDUCTION)
  "Recursion and Induction: Substitutions

  A [3msubstitution[0m  is a set {[3mv_0[0m  <-- [3mt_0[0m, [3mv_1[0m  <-- [3mt_1[0m,  ...} where
  each [3mv_i[0m  is a distinct variable symbol and each [3mt_i[0m  is a term.
  If, for a given substitution [3m\\sigma[0m  and variable [3mv[0m, there is an [3mi[0m
  such that [3mv[0m  is [3mv_i[0m, we say [3mv[0m  [3mis bound[0m  by [3m\\sigma[0m.  If [3mv[0m  is bound
  by [3m\\sigma[0m, then the [3mbinding[0m  of [3mv[0m  in [3m\\sigma[0m  is [3mt_i[0m, for the [3mi[0m
  such that [3mv_i[0m  is [3mv[0m.  (In set theory, a substitution is just a
  finite function that maps the [3mv_i[0m  to their respective [3mt_i[0m.)

  The result of [3mapplying[0m  a substitution [3m\\sigma[0m  to a term [3mterm[0m  is
  denoted [3mterm[0m/[3m\\sigma[0m  and is defined as follows.  If [3mterm[0m is a
  variable, then [3mterm[0m/[3m\\sigma[0m  is either the binding of [3mterm[0m  in
  [3m\\sigma[0m  or is [3mterm[0m  itself, depending on whether [3mterm[0m  is bound in
  [3m\\sigma[0m.  If [3mterm[0m  is a quoted constant, [3mterm[0m/[3m\\sigma[0m  is [3mterm[0m.
  Otherwise, [3mterm[0m  is [47m([0m[3mf[0m  [3ma_1[0m   ...  [3ma_n[0m[47m)[0m and [3mterm[0m/[3m\\sigma[0m  is [47m([0m[3mf[0m
  [3ma_1[0m/[3m\\sigma[0m   ...  [3ma_n[0m/[3m\\sigma[0m[47m)[0m.

  [31;1mProblem 6.
  [0m Suppose [3m\\sigma[0m  is

      {x <-- (car a),
       y <-- (cdr x)}

  What term is [47m(car (cons x (cons y (cons '\"Hello\" z))))[0m/[3m\\sigma[0m?

