 (R-AND-I-TERMS
  (RECURSION-AND-INDUCTION)
  "Recursion and Induction: Terms

  For the purposes of this document, a [3mterm[0m  is a variable symbol, a
  quoted constant, or a function application written as a sequence,
  enclosed in parentheses, consisting of a function symbol of arity [3mn[0m
  followed by [3mn[0m  terms.

  Since [47mcar[0m is a function symbol of arity one and [47mcons[0m is a function
  symbol of arity two, and [47mx[0m and [47my[0m are variable symbols, then [47m(cons
  (car x) y)[0m is a term.  In more conventional notation this term
  would be written [3mcons[0m ([3mcar[0m ([3mx[0m ), [3my[0m ).  We call [47m(car x)[0m and [47my[0m the
  [3mactual expressions[0m  or [3mactuals[0m  of the [3mfunction call[0m  [47m(cons (car x)
  y)[0m.

  Semantically, terms are interpreted with respect to (i) an
  assignment binding variable symbols to constants and (ii) an
  interpretation of function symbols as mathematical functions.  For
  example, suppose the variables [47mx[0m and [47my[0m are bound, respectively, to
  the constants [47m1[0m and [47m(2 3 4)[0m, and suppose the function symbol [47mcons[0m
  is interpreted as the function that constructs ordered pairs (as it
  always is).  Then the meaning or [3mvalue[0m  of the term [47m(cons x y)[0m is
  [47m(1 . (2 3 4))[0m or, equivalently, [47m(1 2 3 4)[0m.  That is, the value of a
  variable is determined by the variable assignment; the value of a
  quoted constant is that constant; and the value of a function
  application, [47m([0m[3mf[0m  [3ma_1[0m  ...  [3ma_n[0m[47m)[0m, is the result of applying the
  mathematical function assigned to [3mf[0m  to the values of the actuals,
  [3ma_i[0m.

  ACL2 provides an infinite number of [3mvariable symbols[0m, whose syntax
  is that of symbols.  Some example variable symbols are [47mx[0m, [47ma1[0m, and
  [47mtemp[0m.  The symbols [47mt[0m and [47mnil[0m are not legal variable symbols.

  A [3mquoted constant[0m  is written by prefixing an integer, a character
  object, a string, or a symbol by a single quote mark.  For example,
  [47m't[0m, [47m'nil[0m, [47m'-3[0m, [47m'[0m[47m#\\A[0m, [47m'\"Hello World!\"[0m and [47m'LOAD[0m are quoted
  constants.  Note that we do not consider [47m'(1 2 3)[0m a quoted
  constant.  This is a mere technicality.  We will shortly introduce
  some abbreviations that allow us to write [47m'(1 2 3)[0m as an
  abbreviation for [47m(cons '1 (cons '2 (cons '3 'nil)))[0m.

  ACL2 also has an infinite number of [3mfunction symbols[0m  each of which
  has an associated [3marity[0m  or number of arguments.  For the moment we
  will concern ourselves with six primitive function symbols: [47mcons[0m,
  [47mcar[0m, [47mcdr[0m, [47mconsp[0m, [47mif[0m, and [47mequal[0m, described below.  Note that we
  implicitly specify the arity of each primitive function symbol.

      [47m(cons [3mx[0m[47m [3my[0m[47m)[0m - construct and return the ordered pair [47m([3mx[0m[47m . [3my[0m[47m)[0m.

      [47m(car [3mx[0m[47m)[0m - return the left component of [3mx[0m, if [3mx[0m  is a pair; otherwise,
      return [47mnil[0m.

      [47m(cdr [3mx[0m[47m)[0m - return the right component of [3mx[0m, if [3mx[0m  is a pair;
      otherwise, return [47mnil[0m.

      [47m(consp [3mx[0m[47m)[0m - return [47mt[0m if [3mx[0m  is a pair; otherwise return [47mnil[0m.

      [47m(if [3mx[0m[47m [3my[0m[47m [3mz[0m[47m)[0m - return [3mz[0m  if [3mx[0m  is [47mnil[0m; otherwise return [3my[0m.

      [47m(equal [3mx[0m[47m [3my[0m[47m)[0m - return [47mt[0m if [3mx[0m  and [3my[0m  are identical; otherwise return
      [47mnil[0m.

  With these primitives we cannot do anything interesting with
  numbers, characters, strings, and symbols.  They are just tokens to
  put into or take out of pairs.  But we can explore most of the
  interesting issues in recursion and induction in this setting!

  (Maybe explore <<[term]>>?)

  Note that if the terms [3m\\alpha[0m and [3m\\beta[0m both evaluate to the same
  value, [3mv[0m, then the term [47m(equal[0m [3m\\alpha[0m [3m\\beta[0m[47m)[0m evaluates to [47mt[0m.  For
  example, the terms [47m(car (cons '3 '4))[0m and [47m'3[0m both evaluate to the
  value [47m3[0m, so the term [47m(equal (car (cons '3 '4)) '3)[0m evaluates to [47mt[0m.

  [31;1mProblem 3.
  [0m Which of the utterances below are terms?

   1. [47m(car (cdr x))[0m

   2. [47m(cons (car x y) z)[0m

   3. [47m(cons 1 2)[0m

   4. [47m(cons '1 '2)[0m

   5. [47m(cons one two)[0m

   6. [47m(cons 'one 'two)[0m

   7. [47m(equal '1 (car (cons '2 '3)))[0m

   8. [47m(if t 1 2)[0m

   9. [47m(if 't '1 '2)[0m

  10. [47m(car (cons (cdr hi-part) (car lo-part)))[0m

  11. [47mcar(cons x y)[0m

  12. [47mcar(cons(x,y))[0m

  13. [47m(cons 1 (2 3 4))[0m

  [31;1mProblem 4.
  [0m For each constant below, write a term whose value is the constant.

   1. [47m((1 . 2) . (3 . 4))[0m

   2. [47m(1 2 3)[0m

   3. [47m((1 . t) (2 . nil) (3 . t))[0m

   4. [47m((A . 1) (B . 2))[0m

  [31;1mProblem 5.
  [0m For each term below, write the constant to which it evaluates.

   1. [47m(cons (cons '1 '2) (cons (cons '3 '4) 'nil))[0m

   2. [47m(cons '1 (cons '2 '3))[0m

   3. [47m(cons 'nil (cons (cons 'nil 'nil) 'nil))[0m

   4. [47m(if 'nil '1 '2)[0m

   5. [47m(if '1 '2 '3)[0m

   6. [47m(equal 'nil (cons 'nil 'nil))[0m

   7. [47m(equal 'Hello 'HELLO)[0m

   8. [47m(equal (cons '1 '2) (cons '1 'two))[0m

