  (ALISTS ACL2-BUILT-INS)
  "Look up value in association list

    General Forms:
    (rassoc x alist)
    (rassoc x alist :test 'eql)   ; same as above (eql as equality test)
    (rassoc x alist :test 'eq)    ; same, but eq is equality test
    (rassoc x alist :test 'equal) ; same, but equal is equality test

  [47m(Rassoc x alist)[0m is the first member of [47malist[0m whose [47m[cdr][0m is [47mx[0m, or
  [47mnil[0m if no such member exists.  [47m(rassoc x alist)[0m is thus similar to
  [47m(assoc x alist)[0m, the difference being that it looks for the first
  pair in the given alist whose [47m[cdr][0m, rather than [47m[car][0m, is [47m[eql][0m to
  [47mx[0m.  See [assoc].  The optional keyword, [47m:TEST[0m, has no effect
  logically, but provides the test (default [47m[eql][0m) used for comparing
  [47mx[0m with the [47m[cdr][0ms of successive elements of [47mlst[0m.

  The [guard] for a call of [47mrassoc[0m depends on the test.  In all cases,
  the second argument must satisfy [47m[alistp][0m.  If the test is [47m[eql][0m,
  then either the first argument must be suitable for [47m[eql][0m (see
  [eqlablep]) or the second argument must satisfy [47m[r-eqlable-alistp][0m.
  If the test is [47m[eq][0m, then either the first argument must be a
  symbol or the second argument must satisfy [47m[r-symbol-alistp][0m.

  See [equality-variants] for a discussion of the relation between
  [47mrassoc[0m and its variants:

      [47m(rassoc-eq x lst)[0m is equivalent to [47m(rassoc x lst :test 'eq)[0m;

      [47m(rassoc-equal x lst)[0m is equivalent to [47m(rassoc x lst :test 'equal)[0m.

  In particular, reasoning about any of these primitives reduces to
  reasoning about the function [47mrassoc-equal[0m.

  [31;1mFunction: [0m<rassoc-equal>

    (defun rassoc-equal (x alist)
      (declare (xargs :guard (alistp alist)))
      (cond ((endp alist) nil)
            ((equal x (cdr (car alist)))
             (car alist))
            (t (rassoc-equal x (cdr alist)))))

