  We next describe how to extend the behavior of [47mreturn-last[0m.  This
  requires an active trust tag (see [defttag]), and is accomplished
  by extending a [table] provided by ACL2, see [return-last-table].
  Rather than using [47m[table][0m [events] directly for this purpose, it is
  probably more convenient to use a macro, [47mdefmacro-last[0m.  We
  describe the community book [47mbooks/misc/profiling.lisp[0m in order to
  illustrate how this works.  The events in that book include the
  following, which are described below.

    (defttag :profiling)

    (progn!
     (set-raw-mode t)
     (load (concatenate 'string (cbd) \"profiling-raw.lsp\")))

    (defmacro-last with-profiling)

