  ACL2 macro [47mwith-profiling[0m, whose calls expand into calls of the
  form [47m(return-last (quote with-profiling-raw) & &)[0m.  The third event
  also extends [47m[return-last-table][0m so that these calls will expand in
  raw Lisp to calls of [47mwith-profiling-raw[0m.

  The example above illustrates the following methodology for
  introducing a macro that returns its last argument but produces
  useful side-effects with raw Lisp code.

      (1) Introduce a trust tag (see [defttag]).

      (2) Using [47m[progn!][0m, load into raw Lisp a file defining a macro,
      [47mRAW-NAME[0m, that takes two arguments, returning its last (second)
      argument but using the first argument to produce desired side
