 (REWRITE-EQUIV
  (REWRITE)
  "Force ACL2 to perform substitution using a stylized [equivalence]
  hypothesis

  [47mRewrite-equiv[0m is actually the [identity] function: [47m(rewrite-equiv x)
  = x[0m for all [47mx[0m.  However, a term of the form [47m(hide (rewrite-equiv
  (equiv x y)))[0m appearing in the hypothesis induces ACL2 to
  aggressively substitute [47my[0m for [47mx[0m when [47mequiv[0m is an [equivalence]
  relation (including [47mequal[0m) and [47mx[0m appears in a context in which
  [47mequiv[0m is being maintained.

  Equivalence relations appearing in the hypothesis are not generally
  used by ACL2 to perform substitutions except under special
  circumstances, such as when one argument is a symbol or a constant
  or during the fertilization stage of the [waterfall] process. A
  stylized [47mrewrite-equiv[0m expression of the form [47m(hide (rewrite-equiv
  (equiv x y)))[0m can be used to override this default behavior.  Care
  should be taken in using [47mrewrite-equiv[0m, however, because it can
  easily result in rewrite loops.

  For an example of a [clause-processor] that leverages [47mRewrite-equiv[0m
  to induce substitution using equivalence relations appearing in the
  hypothesis, see [rewrite-equiv-hint].")
 (REWRITE-IF-AVOID-SWAP
  (REWRITE SYSTEM-ATTACHMENTS)
