 (SET-FC-CRITERIA
  (FORWARD-CHAINING-REPORTS)
  "To set the tracking criteria for forward chaining reports

    Examples:
    (set-fc-criteria)                 ; shut off all tracking
    (set-fc-criteria nil)

    (set-fc-criteria t)               ; to track all forward chaining
    (set-fc-criteria (t t t))

    (set-fc-criteria
     ((:FORWARD-CHAINING LEMMA1)      ; track all uses of LEMMA1,
       t
       t)
      ((:FORWARD-CHAINING LEMMA2)     ; uses of LEMMA2 triggered
       (ALISTP (BASIC-MAPPER A B))    ; by this specific ALISTP term
       t)
      (t t (TRUE-LISTP (DLT D))))     ; and every rule deriving
                                      ; this TRUE-LISTP term.

    General Forms:
    (set-fc-criteria nil)
    (set-fc-criteria t)
    (set-fc-criteria triple1 triple2 ...)

  where each triple is of the form [47m(rune inst-trigger inst-concl)[0m.  If
  rune is non-[47mt[0m is must be a forward chaining [rune].  The other two
  components, [47minst-trigger[0m and [47minst-concl[0m, if non-[47mt[0m, must be terms.
  The list of all the triples supplied is called the ``criteria.'' In
  the form [47m(set-fc-criteria nil)[0m, the criteria used is the empty list
  of triples.  (Technically, supplying [47mnil[0m as a triple ``ought'' to
  be an error, but it is a more ``natural'' way to say the list of
  criteria is empty than to use the correct form [47m(set-fc-criteria)[0m.)
  In the form [47m(set-fc-criteria t)[0m the criteria used is the list
  containing the single triple [47m(t t t)[0m.

  This function sets the tracking criteria for forward chaining
  reporting.  See [forward-chaining-reports] for a general discussion
  of tracking and reporting forward chaining activity.

  Think of the forward chaining criteria as a list of triples,
  representing a disjunction of conjunctions.  The activation of a
  [47m:[0m[47m[forward-chaining][0m rune by some triggering term in the current
  context [3msatisfies[0m the criteria if it satisfies one of the triples.
  To satisfy the triple [47m(rune inst-trigger inst-concl)[0m, the
  activation must satisfy each component of the triple.  Any [47mt[0m
  component is always satisfied.  If [47mrune[0m is non-[47mt[0m it is satisfied if
  the activation is for the given rune.  If [47minst-trigger[0m is non-[47mt[0m, it
  is satisfied if the activation is triggered by the given term.
  (``[47mInst-trigger''[0m stands for ``instantiated trigger.'' It is not
  the trigger term of the rule but is supposed to be an instance of
  that term that you believe will arise in some proof attempt you are
  debugging --- an instance you want to ``watch'' as it fires the
  rule.)  If [47minst-concl[0m is non-[47mt[0m, it is satisfied if the activation
  could possibly derive the conclusion given.  (Again, ``[47minst-concl''[0m
  stands for ``instantiated conclusion'' and shows the term in your
  problem that you expect to be derived by forward chaining.)

  Note that if the criteria is empty, it is never satisfied, so
  tracking is turned off.  If the criteria is the singleton list
  containing just the triple [47m(t t t)[0m, then every activation satisfies
  it and so all [47m:forward chaining[0m rules are tracked.

  See [forward-chaining-reports] for details.")
 (SET-FC-REPORT-ON-THE-FLY
  (FORWARD-CHAINING-REPORTS)
  "To determine when forward-chaining reports are printed

    Examples:  (set-fc-report-on-the-fly t)
               (set-fc-report-on-the-fly nil)

  If the flag is set to [47mt[0m, forward chaining tracking reports are
  printed when forward chaining occurs.  If the flag is set to [47mnil[0m,
  very short reports (giving just the caller and the report number)
  are printed during forward chaining but you can use [47m[fc-report][0m to
  see the full report afterwards.

  Since nothing is tracked when the criteria is [47mnil[0m, this function also
  prints out the current criteria to remind you of what it is.

  The flag manipulated by this function does not shut off tracking.  It
  only determines whether reports are printed on-the-fly or not.  To
  shut off tracking [47m[set-fc-criteria][0m.

  See [forward-chaining-reports] for details.")
