 (SET-LET*-ABSTRACTIONP
  (OUTPUT-CONTROLS)
  "To shorten many prettyprinted [clause]s

  Note: This is an event!  It does not print the usual event [summary]
  but nevertheless changes the ACL2 logical [world] and is so
  recorded.  Moreover, its effect is to set the
  [47m[ACL2-defaults-table][0m, and hence its effect is [47m[local][0m to the book
  or [47m[encapsulate][0m form containing it; see [ACL2-defaults-table].

  When this flag is set to [47mt[0m, subterms that occur more than once in a
  [clause] are abstracted away with [47m[let*][0m, generally shortening the
  displayed size of the clauses.  This flag only affects how clauses
  are printed.  It does not change what terms the theorem prover
  manipulates.

    :set-let*-abstractionp t ;;; or, (set-let*-abstractionp t)

  will cause the prettyprinter to do ``let* abstraction'' on clauses
  before they are printed.  The algorithm finds the maximal
  multiply-occurring subterm and extracts it, binding it to some new
  variable and replacing its occurrences by that variable.  This
  produces a [47mlet*[0m form.  This process is iterated until no subterm
  occurs more than once.  This process generally takes a little time,
  but less time than to print large clauses.  The process can greatly
  reduce the amount of text produced by the prover.

  THIS ONLY AFFECTS HOW THE CLAUSES ARE PRINTED!  The unabstracted
  clauses are manipulated by the theorem prover.

    :set-let*-abstractionp nil

  restores normal clause printing.

  The mode is stored in the defaults table, See [ACL2-defaults-table].
  Thus, the mode may be set locally in books.")
 (SET-MATCH-FREE-DEFAULT
  (FREE-VARIABLES)
  "Provide default for [47m:match-free[0m in future rules

    General Forms:
    (set-match-free-default :once)
    (set-match-free-default :all)
    (set-match-free-default nil)

  Note: This utility does not apply to [type-prescription] rules; for a
  related topic pertinent to such rules, see
  [free-variables-type-prescription].

  As described elsewhere (see [free-variables]), a [rewrite], [linear],
  or [forward-chaining] rule may have free variables in its
  hypotheses, and ACL2 can be directed either to try all bindings
  (``[47m:all[0m'') or just the first (``[47m:once[0m'') when relieving that
  hypothesis, as a basis for relieving subsequent hypotheses.  This
  directing of [47m:all[0m or [47m:once[0m is generally provided by specifying
  either [47m:match-free :once[0m or [47m:match-free :all[0m in the [47m:[0m[47m[rule-classes][0m
  of the rule.  If neither of these is specified, then the most
  recent [47mset-match-free-default[0m is used by ACL2 to fill in this
  missing [47m:match-free[0m field.  See [rule-classes].  Except: If the
  last [47mset-match-free-default[0m specifies [47mnil[0m, then ACL2 reverts to the
  behavior it had at start-up, as described in Remarks (2) and (3)
  below.

  Note: This is an event!  It does not print the usual event [summary]
  but nevertheless changes the ACL2 logical [world] and is so
  recorded.  It uses the [47m[ACL2-defaults-table][0m, and hence its effect
  is [47m[local][0m to the book or [47m[encapsulate][0m form in which it occurs.

  Remarks.

  (1) The use of [47mset-match-free-default[0m has no effect on existing
  rules.  In order to change the behavior of existing rules with
  respect to free-variable matching, see [add-match-free-override].

  (2) If you submit a [rewrite], [linear], or [forward-chaining] rule
  with a free variable in a hypothesis, and no default setting was
  previously specified with [47mset-match-free-default[0m or the default
  setting is [47mnil[0m, and the rule is not within a book being processed
  with [47m[include-book][0m, [47m[certify-book][0m, or [47m[rebuild][0m, then a warning
  or error is caused.  In order to make this an error instead of a
  warning, see [set-match-free-error].

  (3) If you submit a [rewrite], [linear], or [forward-chaining] rule
  with a free variable in a hypothesis, and no default setting has
  been previously specified with [47mset-match-free-default[0m or the
  default setting is [47mnil[0m, and no error is caused (see (2) above),
  then the default [47m:all[0m is used.")
 (SET-MATCH-FREE-ERROR
  (FREE-VARIABLES)
  "Control error vs. warning when [47m:match-free[0m is missing

    Legal Forms:
    (set-match-free-error nil)
    :set-match-free-error nil
    (set-match-free-error t)
    :set-match-free-error t

  As described elsewhere (see [free-variables]), when a [rewrite],
  [linear], or [forward-chaining] rule has free variables in its
  hypotheses, the user can specify whether to try all bindings
  (``[47m:all[0m'') or just the first (``[47m:once[0m'') when relieving its
  hypotheses, as a basis for relieving subsequent hypotheses.  This
  direction of [47m:all[0m or [47m:once[0m is generally provided by specifying
  either [3m:match-free :once[0m or [3m:match-free :all[0m in the [47m:[0m[47m[rule-classes][0m
  of the rule.

  But suppose that neither of these is specified for such a rule.
  (Note: [47mset-match-free-error[0m is not relevant for [type-prescription]
  rules.)  Also suppose that [47mset-match-free-default[0m has not specified
  a default of [47m:once[0m or [47m:all[0m (see [set-match-free-default]).  In this
  case a warning will occur except when in the context of
  [47m[include-book][0m.  If you prefer to see an error in such cases,
  except in the context of [47m[certify-book][0m, execute
  [47m(set-match-free-error t)[0m.  If there is no error, then a default of
  [47m:all[0m is used.

  Note: This is NOT an event!  Instead, [47mset-match-free-error[0m sets the
  state global [47m'match-free-error[0m (see [state] and see [assign]).
  Thus, this form cannot be put into a book.  If you are tempted to
  put it into a book, consider the fact that it really isn't needed
  there, since the absence of [47m:match-free[0m does not cause an error in
  the context of [47m[certify-book][0m or [47m[include-book][0m.  If you still feel
  the need for such a form, consider using [47mset-match-free-default[0m to
  provide a default, at least within the scope of the current book
  (if any); see [set-match-free-default].")
 (SET-MEASURE-FUNCTION
  (DEFUN)
  "Set the default measure function symbol

    Examples:
    (set-measure-function nqthm::count)

  Note: This is an event!  It does not print the usual event [summary]
  but nevertheless changes the ACL2 logical [world] and is so
  recorded.

    General Form:
    (set-measure-function name)

  where [47mname[0m is a function symbol of one argument.  This macro is
  equivalent to [47m(table acl2-defaults-table :measure-function 'name)[0m,
  and hence is [47m[local][0m to any [books] and [47m[encapsulate][0m [events] in
  which it occurs; see [ACL2-defaults-table].  Although this is thus
  an event (see [table]), nevertheless no output results from a
  [47mset-measure-function[0m event.

  This event sets the default measure function to [47mname[0m.  Subsequently,
  if a recursively defined function is submitted to [47m[defun][0m with no
  explicitly given [47m:measure[0m argument, [47m[defun][0m ``guesses'' the measure
  [47m(name var)[0m, where [47mname[0m is the then current default measure function
  and [47mvar[0m is the first formal found to be tested along every branch
  and changed in every recursive call.

  Note that if [47m(table acl2-defaults-table :measure-function 'name)[0m has
  its default value of [47mnil[0m, then the default measure function is
  [47m[ACL2-count][0m.")
