 (SHOW-BDD
  (BDD)
  "Inspect failed BDD proof attempts

  Attempts to use BDDs (see [bdd]), using [47m:[0m[47m[bdd][0m [hints], can fail for
  various reasons.  Sometimes it is useful to explore such failures.
  To do so, one may simply execute the form

    (show-bdd)

  inside the ACL2 loop.  The system's response is generally
  self-explanatory.  Perhaps you have already seen [47mshow-bdd[0m used in
  some examples (see [bdd-introduction] and see [if*]).  Here we give
  some details about [47mshow-bdd[0m.

  [47m(Show-bdd)[0m prints the goal to which the BDD procedure was applied and
  reports the number of nodes created during the [bdd] computation,
  followed by additional information depending on whether or not the
  computation ran to completion or aborted (for reasons explained
  elsewhere; see [bdd-algorithm]).  If the computation did abort, a
  backtrace is printed that should be useful in understanding where
  the problem lies.  Otherwise, [47m(show-bdd)[0m prints out ``falsifying
  constraints.'' This list of pairs associates [term]s with values
  and suggests how to construct a binding list for the variables in
  the conjecture that will falsify the conjecture.  It also prints
  out the [term] that is the result of simplifying the input [term].
  In each of these cases, parts of the object may be hidden during
  printing, in order to avoid creating reams of uninteresting output.
  If so, the user will be queried about whether he wishes to see the
  entire object (alist or [term]), which may be quite large.  The
  following responses are legal:

      [47m w[0m --- Walk around the object with a structure editor

      [47m y[0m --- Print the object in full

      [47m n[0m --- Do not print any more of the object

  [47mShow-bdd[0m actually has four optional arguments, probably rarely used.
  The general form is

    (show-bdd goal-name goal-ans falsifying-ans term-ans)

  where [47mgoal-name[0m is the name of the goal on which the [47m:[0m[47m[bdd][0m hint was
  used (or, [47mnil[0m if the system should find such a goal), [47mgoal-ans[0m is
  [47mnil[0m if there is to be a query and otherwise is the answer to be
  used (without a query) for whether to print the input goal in full
  ([47mt[0m for '[47my[0m', [47mnil[0m for '[47mn[0m', and [47m:w[0m for '[47mw[0m'), [47mfalsifying-ans[0m is the
  answer to be used in place of the query for whether to print the
  falsifying constraints in full, and [47mterm-ans[0m is the answer to be
  used in place of the query for whether to print the resulting
  [term] in full.")
 (SHOW-BODIES
