 (SUBLIS
  (ALISTS ACL2-BUILT-INS)
  "Substitute an alist into a tree

  [47m(Sublis alist tree)[0m is obtained by replacing every leaf of [47mtree[0m with
  the result of looking that leaf up in the association list [47malist[0m.
  However, a leaf is left unchanged if it is not found as a key in
  [47malist[0m.

  Leaves are looked up using the function [47m[assoc][0m.  The [guard] for
  [47m(sublis alist tree)[0m requires [47m(eqlable-alistp alist)[0m.  This [guard]
  ensures that the [guard] for [47m[assoc][0m will be met for each lookup
  generated by [47msublis[0m.

  [47mSublis[0m is defined in Common Lisp.  See any Common Lisp documentation
  for more information.

  [31;1mFunction: [0m<sublis>

    (defun sublis (alist tree)
      (declare (xargs :guard (eqlable-alistp alist)))
      (cond ((atom tree)
             (let ((pair (assoc tree alist)))
               (cond (pair (cdr pair)) (t tree))))
            (t (cons (sublis alist (car tree))
                     (sublis alist (cdr tree))))))")
