  (LISTS STRINGS ACL2-BUILT-INS)
  "Subsequence of a string or list

  For any natural numbers [47mstart[0m and [47mend[0m, where [47mstart[0m [47m<=[0m [47mend[0m [47m<=[0m [47m(length
  seq)[0m, [47m(subseq seq start end)[0m is the subsequence of [47mseq[0m from index
  [47mstart[0m up to, but not including, index [47mend[0m.  [47mEnd[0m may be [47mnil[0m, in
  which case it is treated as though it is [47m(length seq)[0m, i.e., we
  obtain the subsequence of [47mseq[0m from index [47mstart[0m all the way to the
  end.

  The [guard] for [47m(subseq seq start end)[0m is that [47mseq[0m is a true list or
  a string, [47mstart[0m and [47mend[0m are integers (except, [47mend[0m may be [47mnil[0m, in
  which case it is treated as [47m(length seq)[0m for the rest of this
  discussion), and [47m0[0m [47m<=[0m [47mstart[0m [47m<=[0m [47mend[0m [47m<=[0m [47m(length seq)[0m.

  [47mSubseq[0m is a Common Lisp function.  See any Common Lisp documentation
  for more information.  Note: In Common Lisp the third argument of
  [47msubseq[0m is optional, but in ACL2 it is required, though it may be
  [47mnil[0m as explained above.

  [31;1mFunction: [0m<subseq>

    (defun subseq (seq start end)
      (declare (xargs :guard (and (or (true-listp seq) (stringp seq))
                                  (integerp start)
                                  (<= 0 start)
                                  (or (null end)
                                      (and (integerp end)
                                           (<= end (length seq))))
                                  (<= start (or end (length seq))))))
      (if (stringp seq)
          (coerce (subseq-list (coerce seq 'list)
                               start (or end (length seq)))
                  'string)
        (subseq-list seq start (or end (length seq)))))")
