 (SYMBOL<
  (SYMBOLS ACL2-BUILT-INS)
  "Less-than test for symbols

  [47m(symbol< x y)[0m is non-[47mnil[0m if and only if either the [47m[symbol-name][0m of
  the symbol [47mx[0m lexicographically precedes the [47m[symbol-name][0m of the
  symbol [47my[0m (in the sense of [47m[string<][0m) or else the [47m[symbol-name][0ms are
  equal and the [47m[symbol-package-name][0m of [47mx[0m lexicographically precedes
  that of [47my[0m (in the same sense).  So for example, [47m(symbol< 'abcd
  'abce)[0m and [47m(symbol< 'acl2::abcd 'foo::abce)[0m are true.

  The [guard] for [47msymbol[0m specifies that its arguments are symbols.

  [31;1mFunction: [0m<symbol<>

    (defun symbol< (x y)
      (declare (xargs :guard (and (symbolp x) (symbolp y))))
      (let ((x1 (symbol-name x))
            (y1 (symbol-name y)))
        (or (string< x1 y1)
            (and (equal x1 y1)
                 (string< (symbol-package-name x)
                          (symbol-package-name y))))))")
