 (TAKE
  (LISTS ACL2-BUILT-INS)
  "Initial segment (first n elements) of a list

  For any natural number [47mn[0m not exceeding the length of [47ml[0m, [47m(take n l)[0m
  collects the first [47mn[0m elements of the list [47ml[0m.

  The following is a theorem:

    (equal (length (take n l)) (nfix n))

  If [47mn[0m is an integer greater than the length of [47ml[0m, then [47mtake[0m pads the
  list with the appropriate number of [47mnil[0m elements.  Thus, the
  following is also a theorem (though it takes some effort, including
  lemmas, to get ACL2 to prove it).

    (implies (and (integerp n)
                  (true-listp l)
                  (<= (length l) n))
             (equal (take n l)
                    (append l (make-list (- n (length l))))))

  For related functions, see [nthcdr] and see [butlast].

  The [guard] for [47m(take n l)[0m is that [47mn[0m is a nonnegative integer and [47ml[0m
  is a true list.

  [31;1mFunction: [0m<first-n-ac>

    (defun first-n-ac (i l ac)
      (declare (type (integer 0 *) i)
               (xargs :guard (and (true-listp l) (true-listp ac))))
      (cond ((zp i) (revappend ac nil))
            (t (first-n-ac (1- i)
                           (cdr l)
                           (cons (car l) ac)))))

  [31;1mFunction: [0m<take>

    (defun take (n l)
      (declare (xargs :guard (and (integerp n)
                                  (not (< n 0))
                                  (true-listp l))))
      (mbe :logic
           (if (zp n)
               nil
             (cons (car l) (take (1- n) (cdr l))))
           :exec (first-n-ac n l nil)))")
