 (TERM-LIST-LISTP
  (ACL2-BUILT-INS)
  "recognizer for a list of [clause]s

    Example:
    (term-list-listp
     '(((NOT (ENDP X)) (NATP (LEN X)))
       ((ENDP X) (NOT (NATP (LEN (CDR X)))) (NATP (LEN X))))
     (w state))

    General Form:
    (term-list-listp x w)

  where [47mx[0m is any ACL2 object and [47mw[0m is an ACL2 logical [world].  The
  result is [47mt[0m or [47mnil[0m according to whether [47mx[0m is a true list of true
  lists of quotations of well-formed terms in [47mw[0m.

  This function is the standard ACL2 idiom for recognizing a ``set of
