 (TOGGLE-INHIBIT-ER
  (OUTPUT-CONTROLS ERRORS)
  "Add or delete an error output string from the [47minhibit-er-table[0m

  See [set-inhibit-er] for relevant background.

    General Form:
    (toggle-inhibit-er string)

  where [47mstring[0m is the name of some error output like [47m\"Translate\"[0m or
  [47m\"Failure\"[0m.

  Note: This is an event!  It does not print the usual event [summary]
  but nevertheless changes the ACL2 logical [world] and is so
  recorded.  It is [47m[local][0m to the book or [47m[encapsulate][0m form in which
  it occurs; see [toggle-inhibit-er!] for a corresponding non-[47m[local][0m
  event.  Indeed, [47m(toggle-inhibit-er str)[0m is equivalent to [47m(local
  (toggle-inhibit-er! str))[0m.

  The given string is added to the list of strings used for inhibiting
  error output if it is not there already and is deleted from the
  list if it is there.  Case is unimportant in [47mstring[0m.  See
  [47m[set-inhibit-er][0m.")
 (TOGGLE-INHIBIT-ER!
  (OUTPUT-CONTROLS ERRORS)
  "Toggle an [47minhibit-er-table[0m entry non-[47m[local][0mly

  Please see [toggle-inhibit-er], which is the same as
  [47mtoggle-inhibit-er![0m except that the latter is not [47m[local][0m to the
  [47m[encapsulate][0m or the book in which it occurs.  Probably
  [toggle-inhibit-er] is to be preferred unless you have a good
  reason for wanting to export the effect of this event outside the
  enclosing [47m[encapsulate][0m or book.")
 (TOGGLE-INHIBIT-WARNING
  (OUTPUT-CONTROLS)
  "Add or delete a warning string from the [47minhibit-warnings-table[0m

    General Form:
    (toggle-inhibit-warning string)

  where [47mstring[0m is the name of some warning like [47m\"Subsume\"[0m, [47m\"Non-rec\"[0m or
  [47m\"Rewrite-lambda-object\"[0m.

  Note: This is an event!  It does not print the usual event [summary]
  but nevertheless changes the ACL2 logical [world] and is so
  recorded.  It is [47m[local][0m to the book or [47m[encapsulate][0m form in which
  it occurs; see [toggle-inhibit-warning!] for a corresponding
  non-[47m[local][0m event.  Indeed, [47m(toggle-inhibit-warning str)[0m is
  equivalent to [47m(local (toggle-inhibit-warning! str))[0m.

  The given string is added to the list of inhibited warnings if it is
  not there already and is deleted from the list if it is there.
  Case is unimportant in [47mstring[0m.  See [47m[set-inhibit-warnings][0m.")
