 (TOP-LEVEL
  (MISCELLANEOUS)
  "Evaluate a top-level form as a function body

  Some forms, such as calls of [47m[with-local-stobj][0m, are illegal when
  supplied directly to the ACL2 top-level loop.  The macro [47mtop-level[0m
  provides a workaround in such cases, by defining a temporary
  [47m:[0m[47m[program][0m-mode function named [47mtop-level-fn[0m whose only argument is
  [47mstate[0m and whose body is the form to be evaluated.  When the call of
  [47mtop-level[0m returns there is no change to the existing ACL2 logical
  [world].  The following edited log illustrates all of the above
  points.

    ACL2 !>:pbt 0
              0  (EXIT-BOOT-STRAP-MODE)
    ACL2 !>(defstobj st fld)

    Summary
    Form:  ( DEFSTOBJ ST ...)
    Rules: NIL
    Time:  0.01 seconds (prove: 0.00, print: 0.00, other: 0.01)
     ST
    ACL2 !>(top-level
            (with-local-stobj
             st
             (mv-let (result st)
                     (let ((st (update-fld 17 st)))
                       (mv (fld st) st))
                     result)))
    17
    ACL2 !>(top-level
            (with-local-stobj
             st
             (mv-let (result st)
                     (let ((st (update-fld 17 st)))
                       (mv (fld st) st))
                     (mv nil result state))))
     17
    ACL2 !>(top-level
            (with-local-stobj
             st
             (mv-let (result st)
                     (let ((st (update-fld 17 st)))
                       (mv (fld st) st))
                     (mv result state))))
    (17 <state>)
    ACL2 !>:pbt 0
              0  (EXIT-BOOT-STRAP-MODE)
       d      1:x(DEFSTOBJ ST FLD)
    ACL2 !>

  Each argument of [47mtop-level[0m after the first should be a [47m[declare][0m form
  or [documentation] string, as the list of these extra arguments
  will be placed before the first argument when forming the
  definition of [47mtop-level-fn[0m.

  [47m[Top-level][0m generates a call of [47m[ld][0m, so that the value returned is
  printed in the normal way.  The call of [47m[top-level][0m itself actually
  evaluates to [47m(mv erp :invisible state)[0m, where [47merp[0m is [47mt[0m if and only
  evaluation of the call of [47mtop-level-fn[0m caused an error, which
  normally results in no additional output.  (For details about
  ``caused an error'', see the definition of [47mtop-level[0m in the ACL2
  source code, and see [ld-error-action].)

  Since the defined function [47mtop-level[0m takes only [47mstate[0m as a parameter,
  the given form should not include any user-defined [stobj]s that
  occur free in the form.

  Finally, note that since [47mtop-level[0m runs a function that is defined in
  [47m:[0m[47m[program][0m mode, it is possible for a raw lisp error to occur.
  Here is an example.

    ACL2 !>(top-level (car 3))

    ***********************************************
    ************ ABORTING from raw Lisp ***********
    ********** (see :DOC raw-lisp-error) **********
    Error:  The value 3 is not of the expected type LIST.
    While executing: CAR
    ***********************************************")
