 (UNSIGNED-BYTE-P
  (NUMBERS ACL2-BUILT-INS)
  "Recognizer for natural numbers that fit in a specified bit width

  [47m(Unsigned-byte-p bits x)[0m is [47mT[0m when [47mbits[0m is a positive integer and [47mx[0m
  is a nonnegative integer that fits into a bit-width of [47mbits[0m, i.e.,
  [47m0 <= x < 2^bits[0m.

  Note that a [type-spec] of [47m(unsigned-byte i)[0m for a variable [47mx[0m in a
  function's [47m[declare][0m form translates to a [guard] condition of
  [47m(unsigned-byte-p i x)[0m.

  The [guard] for [47munsigned-byte-p[0m is [47mT[0m.

  [31;1mFunction: [0m<unsigned-byte-p>

    (defun unsigned-byte-p (bits x)
      (declare (xargs :guard t))
