  to execute more efficiently than [47m(equal x 0)[0m in properly [guard]ed
  compiled code.

  In recursions down the natural numbers, [47m(zp x)[0m is preferred over
  [47m(zerop x)[0m because the former coerces [47mx[0m to a natural and allows the
  termination proof.  In recursions through the integers, [47m(zip x)[0m is
  preferred.  See [zero-test-idioms].

  [47mZerop[0m is a Common Lisp function.  See any Common Lisp documentation
  for more information.

  [31;1mFunction: [0m<zerop>

    (defun zerop (x)
      (declare (xargs :guard (acl2-numberp x)))
      (eql x 0))")
 (ZIP
